repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-05T23:02:23Z","updated_at":"2026-05-05T23:02:23Z","body":"I can confirm this on 4.7.beta https://github.com/godotengine/godot/commit/1f012286cf9321b2209259539d1e638dac4eed73 on a double-precision build (Linux + NVIDIA).\n\nI bisected the regression to https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111183. cc @stuartcarnie \n\nAdditionally, in certain engine sessions, grass will flicker and change its height when the camera moves (and also disappear at certain camera angles). Sometimes, the grass will merely disappear at certain camera angles, but not flicker or change its height when the camera moves. This could point to this being due to an uninitialized memory issue.\n\n⚠️ Video below contains flashing images. ⚠️ \n\n<details>\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5700d2a8-e1b6-4a46-86f9-e84ebb38bbf0\n</details>\n\n> Changed h265 videos to h264. Quality is degraded, but it should play on everyone's devices now. I thought GitHub would stream regardless of encoding. Didn't realize that wasn't the case.\n\nPS: [AV1 support](https://caniuse.com/av1) (in the `.webm` container at least) is nearly universal nowadays, so it's safe to use on GitHub. It achieves comparable quality to H.265, but works in all modern browsers. I've regularly uploaded AV1 videos to GitHub and didn't get any reports of videos not playing so far.\n\nVP9 is even more universal, since it also works on Safari on old macOS versions or devices (prior to M3 and A16 processors), but it's only slightly better than H.264.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4383775712/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confus